> You haven't set up xterm properly (or the menu item) to emulate the pc
> character set - it's probably doing vt220.

When I played on UNIX in an xterm, I would do this in ksh or bash:

TERM=xterm
export TERM
tset -r

Or this in csh

setenv TERM xterm
tset -r

Then just to double check I would resize my xterm or hpterm window.

BTW, if you're getting this type of display problem with Nethack you
are also getting it using vi.  Watch out for incorrect text files.



